# SlayZone Chromium — Execution Plan

Ground-up migration of every SlayZone surface onto a Chromium fork + Bun sidecar. Organized so every surface currently in the app has a named home in a named phase, every phase ends with something testable, and foundations land before surfaces.

Architecture reference: [Implementation plan](asset:978a4843) · [Migration investigation](asset:3cd6fdf1).

**Principles**
- Foundations before surfaces. No UI migration until the shell + IPC + state transport are stable.
- Each phase ends with a demo — a user-visible artifact a human can click through.
- Parity-tested per surface: for every migrated screen, a side-by-side diff vs. the Electron build must pass before the old path is deleted.
- 119 `ipcMain.handle` calls + 19 domain packages are tracked on a parity ledger. Not a single handler or component is allowed to slip through.
- Continuous activities (upstream merge bot, parity ledger, CI health) run alongside phase work from day one of the phase that introduces them.

