# Part I — Foundations (Phases 1–6)

## Phase 1 — Build infrastructure

Stand up Chromium build tooling before writing any patch. Everything downstream assumes reproducible builds on Mac + Linux + Windows.

- **1.1 Install `depot_tools`** — Google's build toolkit (`gclient`, `gn`, `ninja`, `autoninja`). Verified via `which gclient`.
- **1.2 Fetch Chromium source** — `fetch --nohooks chromium` + `gclient sync`. Baseline ~50 GB.
- **1.3 Verify baseline build** — `autoninja -C out/Default chrome` produces a runnable binary on all three OSes.
- **1.4 Provision `reclient` cluster** — distributed build cache. Target: full build < 30 min, incremental < 5 min.
- **1.5 CI matrix scaffolding** — runners for Mac×2 arch, Win×2 arch, Linux×2 arch with `depot_tools` + `reclient` baked in.
- **1.6 Signing pipeline stubs** — Apple Developer ID + notarization, Azure Key Vault for Win EV, GPG for Linux. Dry-run only.
- **1.7 Smoke-test `chrome://hello/` page with a button** — throwaway patch proving the full chain: build → sign → launch → custom scheme → JS.

**Phase 1 demo**: launch signed binary, navigate to `chrome://hello/`, click the button, counter ticks.

**Exit**: all three OSes build + sign in CI; `chrome://hello/` clickable on each.

