## Phase 2 — Foundation patches

Only the patches needed to host WebUIs + talk to the sidecar. UI-tree patches are deferred to Phase 5; inline-tab patch to Phase 6.

- **2.1 Branding** — name, icon, about page, splash. Mechanical.
- **2.2 `chrome://` scheme handler factory** — one registration per region; replaces the throwaway from 1.7.
- **2.3 IPC bridge C++ shim** — `SlayzoneSidecarClient`: Unix socket, JSON-RPC request/response, keepalive, reconnect.
- **2.4 Telemetry strip** — compile out UMA, Crashpad upload, Safe Browsing phone-home, field trials.
- **2.5 NTP override** — default new tab → `chrome://slayzone-shell/` (empty placeholder for now).

**Phase 2 demo**: signed binary launches, NTP shows the (empty) shell, sidecar connection handshakes (logged).

**Exit**: all five patches in the patch series, clean rebase onto latest Chromium stable tag.

