## Phase 3 — Bun sidecar extraction

Lift `packages/apps/app/src/main/` into a standalone Bun process. Hard dependency: **every** `ipcMain.handle` call must have a JSON-RPC counterpart. This is the most mechanical phase but also the one with the most breadth — 119 handlers across 6 files.

- **3.1 Inventory + parity ledger** — automated scan of `ipcMain.handle(...)` → CSV: method, file, arity, return type, domain. Ledger becomes the phase-complete checklist.
- **3.2 Factor `main/` into a pure Node module** — strip `electron` imports. Internal interfaces replace `app` / `BrowserWindow` / `ipcMain` touchpoints.
- **3.3 JSON-RPC method registry** — decorator or manifest file. Auto-generates the dispatch map + TS client types (shared with `packages/shared/rpc-types/`).
- **3.4 Unix socket server** — `$SLAYZONE_RUNTIME_DIR/sidecar.sock`. Multiplexed requests, crash recovery, reconnect.
- **3.5 Native-module compat** — verify `better-sqlite3`, `node-pty`, `@convex/browser`, `express`, `ws`, `msgpackr` under Bun. Fall back to Node via `SLAYZONE_RUNTIME=node` if any blocks.
- **3.6 Proxy Electron-only APIs** — `dialog`, `Menu`, `globalShortcut`, `Notification`, `autoUpdater` → each becomes a JSON-RPC method answered by the C++ shim from 2.3.
- **3.7 Sidecar lifecycle** — Chromium launches sidecar on startup, tears it down on exit. Respawn + state replay on crash.
- **3.8 Parity verification** — Electron build still runs, but pointed at the new sidecar via a compatibility shim. All 119 handlers reply correctly. Ledger is 100% green.
- **3.9 Handler test migration to Bun** — port every `main/**/*.test.ts` (handlers, DB migrations, state machines, backup/export, floating-agent state) to run under the sidecar's Vitest-on-Bun setup. Replace Electron stubs with sidecar-internal equivalents. Tests in the test-coverage ledger (C5) flip from `electron` to `bun`.
- **3.10 Preload test replacement** — delete `preload/**/*.test.ts`; reimplement equivalents as RPC-client tests in `packages/shared/rpc-client/` (in Phase 4.7). Tracked in C5 as `replaced-in-4.7`.

**Phase 3 demo**: current Electron SlayZone runs unchanged against the Bun sidecar via a shim. No user-visible difference. Every handler test passes under Bun.

**Exit**: parity ledger 100% green; existing Playwright suite passes; every migrated handler test green on Bun; preload tests fully retired from ledger.

