## Phase 5 — Native layout shell

Empty `views::` tree that will host the WebUIs. No region content yet — placeholder WebViews.

- **5.1 `SlayzoneBrowserView` subclass** — root `views::View`, BoxLayout tree, member WebView pointers per region slot.
- **5.2 Layout slots** — one WebView per region slot, each loading a placeholder `chrome://slayzone-placeholder/?region=<name>` that renders its name + size.
- **5.3 Feasibility checkpoint (inline-tab smoke)** — before wiring the rest of the layout, drop one real-browser `WebContents` from `TabStripModel` into a single layout slot via `WebView::SetWebContents`. Does it render? Does it resize with the parent? Does it handle focus? If yes → continue. If no → stop and redesign before investing in the full layout. This is the de-risking that a throwaway spike would have tried to do, now inside the real code path with no duplication.
- **5.4 `views::SplitView`** — draggable terminal ↔ browser divider, snap points, keyboard resize.
- **5.5 `views::FocusManager` plumbing** — tab cycle between regions, shortcut routing: region → Mojo → browser proc → target region.
- **5.6 Layout intent API** — regions send `hide`/`show`/`resize` via Mojo; browser proc calls `SetVisible` / triggers reflow.

**Phase 5 demo**: launch binary, see the full layout grid with labelled placeholders + one slot showing a real web page, drag the split, tab through regions.

**Exit**: every slot reachable; 5.3 checkpoint passed (real `WebContents` renders + resizes + focuses in a slot); resize stable; focus cycles correctly.

