# Part II — Surface migration (Phases 7–15)

Each phase migrates one category of surfaces onto real chrome:// WebUIs. A surface is not considered migrated until parity testing (A/B vs. Electron build) passes.

**Tests travel with code.** Every surface phase has an explicit `.T` step: port the matching `*.test.ts(x)` files from `apps/app/src/renderer/**` (and any relevant `domains/*/client/**`) into the new WebUI package; update imports; verify green under the Phase 4.7 shared harness. No surface counts as migrated until its tests pass at the new location. Status is tracked per file on the C5 ledger.

## Phase 7 — Task-detail regions

The main working surface of SlayZone — what's in the screenshot. Ten regions.

- **7.1 `chrome://slayzone-shell/`** — outer frame, owns cross-region routing state.
- **7.2 `chrome://slayzone-tabbar/`** — top task tabs (current `TabBar.tsx`).
- **7.3 `chrome://slayzone-projects/`** — left project icon rail (current `AppSidebar.tsx` slim side).
- **7.4 `chrome://slayzone-tasklist/`** — kanban + list view (`KanbanBoard`, `KanbanListView`, `FilterBar`).
- **7.5 `chrome://slayzone-sidebar/`** — task metadata sidebar (descriptions, tags, priority).
- **7.6 `chrome://slayzone-taskheader/`** — task title row + status selector.
- **7.7 `chrome://slayzone-terminal/`** — xterm.js panel (near-verbatim port; terminal domain unchanged).
- **7.8 `chrome://slayzone-browserchrome/`** — URL bar + nav buttons wired to Phase 6.3.
- **7.9 `chrome://slayzone-tools/`** — right-side tool toggles.
- **7.10 `chrome://slayzone-statusbar/`** — bottom status.
- **7.11 Parity gate** — A/B screenshot diff per region; state sync across regions verified under load.
- **7.T Test port** — move renderer component tests for `TabBar`, kanban, filter bar, task detail, task header, sidebar into their new WebUI packages. All green under 4.7 harness. C5 rows updated.

**Phase 7 demo**: open a task, see the full detail view, interact with kanban, terminal, inline browser. Feature-complete vs. Electron for task flow.

**Exit**: parity passes all ten regions; task-open flow indistinguishable from Electron build.

