## Phase 10 — Dialog framework + core dialogs

Dialogs need their own shared infra — a lightweight dialog host WebUI + a dialog-open Mojo channel. Then the core dialogs migrate.

- **10.1 `chrome://slayzone-dialogs/`** — dialog host. Receives `(dialogId, props)` via Mojo, renders the matching component, returns result.
- **10.2 `CreateTaskDialog` + `EditTaskDialog` + `DeleteTaskDialog`** — task lifecycle.
- **10.3 `CreateProjectDialog` + `ProjectSettingsDialog` + `DeleteProjectDialog`** — project lifecycle.
- **10.4 `SearchDialog`** — Cmd+K global search.
- **10.5 `FeedbackDialog` + `CliInstallDialog` + `ChangelogDialog`** — auxiliary.
- **10.6 Modal focus trap + ESC handling** — `views::Widget` modal mode, focus return.
- **10.7 Parity gate** — open, interact, submit for every dialog.
- **10.T Test port** — `CliInstallDialog.test.tsx` + any dialog-specific tests from `tasks`/`projects` domains move into the dialogs WebUI. New tests for the dialog host (dialogId routing, result return). All green. C5 updated.

**Phase 10 demo**: every dialog openable via keyboard shortcut and sidebar menu; identical to Electron.

**Exit**: all ~10 core dialogs pass parity.

