# Part III — Cross-cutting (Phases 16–19)

## Phase 16 — Auth + updates

Things that span every surface.

- **16.1 Convex auth** — login flow migrated; tokens stored by sidecar, never in renderer.
- **16.2 Session rotation** — Chromium browser session shared across WebUIs via cookie domain.
- **16.3 Auto-update** — Sparkle (Mac) / Squirrel-like (Win) / AppImage updater (Linux), driven by sidecar, surfaced in settings.
- **16.4 Crash reporting** — replace stripped Crashpad with SlayZone-owned sink (sidecar).

**Exit**: login, logout, session expiry, update prompt, update apply — all work.

---

## Phase 17 — Keyboard, focus, zen mode

The polish pass. The existing app has strong keyboard + zen rules (many feedback memories about shortcut routing, focus quirks) — preserve all of them.

- **17.1 Shortcut matrix** — every registered shortcut mapped: which WebUI owns it, which is native menu, which is global.
- **17.2 Native menu accelerators** — Chromium's real OS menu replaces current react-hotkeys for menu-bound shortcuts.
- **17.3 Focus chain** — `lastFocusedPanelRef` behavior ported via browser-proc tracking of WebView focus.
- **17.4 Zen mode** — full-screen single-region mode; hide chrome, hide status, hide tools.
- **17.5 Parity gate** — full shortcut matrix passes automated + manual tests.

**Exit**: every shortcut from the existing app works identically.

---

## Phase 18 — Full-suite test retarget

Playwright currently drives Electron; unit/integration tests were migrated per-surface in Phases 3.9, 4.7, and the `.T` steps of Phases 7–15. This phase assembles the full picture, retargets the top-level runners, and gates the parity suite.

- **18.1 Playwright Chromium driver** — swap `electron.launch` for `chromium.launch`; fixtures updated for `chrome://` URLs.
- **18.2 Port existing e2e/ specs** — every `packages/apps/app/e2e/core/*.spec.ts` runs against the new binary. Specs that test Electron-specific behavior (BrowserWindow, `webContents.send`, etc.) get rewritten against the new architecture.
- **18.3 Parity screenshot suite** — per-region baselines consolidated from Phases 7–15; diff threshold calibrated.
- **18.4 Load tests** — 200 tasks, 50 tabs, 10 open browsers. Measure TTI + frame drops.
- **18.5 Flake budget** — <1% flake over 100 runs.
- **18.6 CLI test verification** — `packages/apps/cli/test/*.test.ts` run against the Bun sidecar (not Electron main). Domain/handler tests (already on Bun from 3.9) join the full-suite CI run.
- **18.7 Coverage gate** — per-package threshold (initially current %, never lower). C5 ledger fully green: every original test file is either passing in its new home or explicitly retired with reason.

**Exit**: full unit + integration + CLI + e2e suites all green on the Chromium binary; parity suite green; C5 ledger 100% reconciled.

